<div class="page">

  <h1>Desk Buddy &mdash; Connection Schematics</h1>
  <p class="sub">Two builds: <b>normal ESP32 DevKit</b> &middot; <b>ESP32 Mini (C3 / small dev board)</b>
     &mdash; powered by USB 5&nbsp;V, everything else 3V3</p>

  <div class="note danger">
    <b>Read this first.</b> Build one module at a time and test before adding the next.
    Never put 5&nbsp;V into a 3V3 pin. Sensor + OLED + touch run on 3V3; only the audio amp
    and the motor supply may use 5&nbsp;V.
  </div>

  <div class="legend">
    <span><span class="chip r">RED</span> 3V3 power</span>
    <span><span class="chip k">BLACK</span> GND</span>
    <span><span class="chip g">GREEN</span> SDA / I2C data</span>
    <span><span class="chip b">BLUE</span> SCL / I2C clock</span>
    <span><span class="chip p">PURPLE</span> mic out</span>
    <span><span class="chip o">ORANGE</span> touch out</span>
    <span><span class="chip c">CYAN</span> audio</span>
    <span><span class="chip y">YELLOW</span> motor PWM</span>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================ DEV BOARD -->
  <h2><span class="badge dev">Board 1</span> Normal ESP32 DevKit (30 / 38-pin, e.g. ESP-WROOM-32)</h2>

