  <!-- ============================================================ ESP32 MINI -->
  <h2><span class="badge mini">Board 2</span> ESP32 Mini (ESP32-C3 / small dev board)</h2>

  <p>Use this build for a small C3 / mini board (USB-C, fewer pins). <b>Two differences that
     matter:</b></p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>No DAC.</b> The classic GPIO25 DAC does not exist, so audio is generated with
        <code>ledcWriteTone()</code> (a PWM square wave) on a normal GPIO. Sound is thinner but
        it works.</li>
    <li><b>Fewer exposed pins.</b> Prefer GPIO4/5 for I2C (many mini boards default to SDA=GPIO8,
        SCL=GPIO9 &mdash; either is fine, just stay consistent in the sketch).</li>
  </ul>

