  <h2>Sketch changes for the Mini (C3)</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>What</th><th>DevKit version</th><th>Mini / C3 version</th></tr>
    <tr><td>I2C pins</td><td><code>SDA=21, SCL=22</code></td><td><code>SDA=8, SCL=9</code> (or 4/5)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Mic input</td><td><code>GPIO35</code></td><td><code>GPIO2</code> (ADC1)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Touch input</td><td><code>GPIO32</code></td><td><code>GPIO3</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Motor PWM</td><td><code>GPIO27</code></td><td><code>GPIO7</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Audio out</td><td><code>GPIO25</code> real DAC</td><td><code>GPIO6</code> PWM tone</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Board</td><td><code>esp32</code></td><td><code>esp32c3</code></td></tr>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    For audio on the C3, replace the DAC write with a tone generator:
    <pre style="background:#1f2430;color:#eef0ff;border-radius:8px;padding:12px;font-size:12.5px;overflow-x:auto">
// ESP32-C3: no DAC, make a tone with LEDC PWM
ledcSetup(0, 2000, 8);              // pin, 2 kHz, 8-bit
ledcAttachPin(6, 0);                // tone out on GPIO6
ledcWrite(0, 128);                  // square wave &#8594; amp L input
    </pre>
    Swap pin <code>6</code>, channel <code>0</code>, and the values as needed. Everything else in the
    existing sketches stays the same apart from the pin numbers above.
  </div>

  <h2>Power summary (both boards)</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Rail</th><th>Source</th><th>Feeds</th></tr>
    <tr><td><span class="chip r">5 V</span></td><td>USB (board VIN / VBUS)</td><td>HXJ8002 amp only</td></tr>
    <tr><td><span class="chip r">3V3</span></td><td>board regulator out</td><td>OLED, ToF, mic, touch, motor</td></tr>
    <tr><td><span class="chip k">GND</span></td><td>board ground</td><td>every module (common ground)</td></tr>
  </table>

  <div class="note danger">
    <b>Safety:</b> all modules share one common ground. Power the amp from 5&nbsp;V but tie its
    GND to the board GND. Do not back-feed 5&nbsp;V into the 3V3 rail. Disconnect USB before
    rewiring the motor or amp.
  </div>

